(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test10_1B"] = [{"id":"a0777403","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The following text is from Anita Desai’s 2011 novella Translator Translated. While working on her translation of a novel written in Odia (a language of India) into English, the narrator looks out her window at night to clear her mind. I tried to distract myself with these sights of the ordinary world, but in my mind it was the lines I had been translating and the lines that I had been writing that remained in the forefront. I longed for sleep to obliterate them but it eluded me. Perhaps everything would be normal again once I had sent off the manuscript, I thought, and looked forward to completing the work. ©2011 by Anita Desai As used in the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Anita Desai’s 2011 novella Translator Translated. While working on her translation of a novel written in Odia (a language","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of India) into English, the narrator looks out her window at night to clear her mind.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"I tried to distract myself with these sights of the ordinary world, but in my mind it was the lines I had been translating and the lines","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"that I had been writing that remained in the forefront. I longed for sleep to obliterate them but it eluded me. Perhaps everything","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"would be normal again once I had sent off the manuscript, I thought, and looked forward to completing the work.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"©2011 by Anita Desai","indent":4}],"question":"As used in the text, what does the word “completing” most nearly mean?","choices":["Destroying","Finishing","Advertising","Rejecting"],"underline":"completing","underline_segments":["completing"]},{"id":"a68239ed","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Oscar Wilde’s 1897 nonfiction work De Profundis. People whose desire is solely for self-realisation never know where they are going. They can’t know. In one sense of the word it is of course necessary to know oneself: that is the first achievement of knowledge. But to recognise that the soul of a man is unknowable, is the ultimate achievement of wisdom. The final mystery is oneself. When one has weighed the sun in the balance, and measured the steps of the moon, and mapped out the seven heavens star by star, there still remains oneself. Who can calculate the orbit of his own soul?","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Oscar Wilde’s 1897 nonfiction work De Profundis.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"People whose desire is solely for self-realisation never know where they are going. They can’t know. In one sense of the word it is","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"of course necessary to know oneself: that is the first achievement of knowledge. But to recognise that the soul of a man is","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"unknowable, is the ultimate achievement of wisdom. The final mystery is oneself. When one has weighed the sun in the balance,","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"and measured the steps of the moon, and mapped out the seven heavens star by star, there still remains oneself. Who can","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"calculate the orbit of his own soul?","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined question in the text as a whole?","choices":["It reinforces the text’s skepticism about the possibility of truly achieving self-knowledge.","It speculates that some readers will share the doubts expressed in the text about the value of self-knowledge.","It cautions readers that the text’s directions for how to achieve self-knowledge are hard to follow.","It concedes that the definition of self-knowledge advanced in the text is unpopular."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Who can","calculate the orbit of his own soul?"]},{"id":"4974b053","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Although science fiction was dominated mostly by white male authors when Octavia Butler, a Black woman, began writing, she did not view the genre as ______: Butler broke into the field with the publication of several short stories and her 1976 novel Patternmaster, and she later became the first science fiction writer to win a prestigious MacArthur Fellowship.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Although science fiction was dominated mostly by white male authors when Octavia Butler, a Black woman, began writing, she did not view the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"genre as ______: Butler broke into the field with the publication of several short stories and her 1976 novel Patternmaster, and she later became","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the first science fiction writer to win a prestigious MacArthur Fellowship.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["legitimate","impenetrable","compelling","indecipherable"]},{"id":"7b43c0cc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Steiger Butte Drum, a family ensemble from the Klamath Tribes of the Pacific Northwest, collaborated with composer Michael Gordon to create Natural History, a work featuring traditional drumming and vocals alongside an orchestra and chorus. Steiger Butte Drum’s participation is ______ to the piece: members not only contributed to its composition but also must be included in all performances.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Steiger Butte Drum, a family ensemble from the Klamath Tribes of the Pacific Northwest, collaborated with composer Michael Gordon to create","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Natural History, a work featuring traditional drumming and vocals alongside an orchestra and chorus. Steiger Butte Drum’s participation is ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to the piece: members not only contributed to its composition but also must be included in all performances.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["tangential","subsequent","analogous","integral"]},{"id":"662ebff2","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In response to concerns that some recent financial crises were exacerbated by consumers misunderstanding risks associated with credit cards, loans, and other financial products, policymakers in many countries have instituted risk-disclosure requirements on sellers of those products. Enrique Seira et al. investigated a variety of risk-disclosure messages sent to thousands of credit card customers and found that the messages had only small and short-lived effects on behavior. Seira et al. asserted that such effects may nevertheless be worth pursuing, given the negligible cost of messaging.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In response to concerns that some recent financial crises were exacerbated by consumers misunderstanding risks associated with credit cards,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"loans, and other financial products, policymakers in many countries have instituted risk-disclosure requirements on sellers of those products.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Enrique Seira et al. investigated a variety of risk-disclosure messages sent to thousands of credit card customers and found that the messages","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"had only small and short-lived effects on behavior. Seira et al. asserted that such effects may nevertheless be worth pursuing, given the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"negligible cost of messaging.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It notes a factor that led Seira et al. to not dismiss risk-disclosure messaging altogether despite their evidence of its limited utility.","It acknowledges a type of risk-disclosure messaging that Seira et al. may not have fully accounted for in their study.","It describes a consideration that explains why Seira et al. recommended risk-disclosure messaging even though its effects may be small relative to its costs.","It points out a circumstance that Seira et al. conceded may make risk-disclosure messaging more effective than their study suggests."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["given the","negligible cost of messaging."]},{"id":"e386a11d","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Cat and Plum Blossoms is an important work of Nihonga, or classical Japanese painting. Unlike Kuroda Seiki, who adopted traditional European methods such as painting with oil on canvas, Hishida Shuns ō ______ traditional Japanese approaches. For instance, Hishida produced Cat and Plum Blossoms by applying color pigments to a silk scroll.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Cat and Plum Blossoms is an important work of Nihonga, or classical Japanese painting. Unlike Kuroda Seiki, who adopted traditional European","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"methods such as painting with oil on canvas, Hishida Shunsō ______ traditional Japanese approaches. For instance, Hishida produced Cat and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Plum Blossoms by applying color pigments to a silk scroll.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["distrusted","embraced","released","overlooked"]},{"id":"7a0e31ea","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Betty Smith’s 1943 novel A Tree Grows in Brooklyn. Francie, a young girl, visits the library often. Francie thought that all the books in the world were in that library and she had a plan about reading all the books in the world. She was reading a book a day in alphabetical order and not skipping the dry ones. She remembered that the first author had been Abbott. She had been reading a book a day for a long time now and she was still in the B’s. Already she had read about bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations and Byzantine architecture. For all her enthusiasm, she had to admit that some of the B’s had been’ hard going. But Francie was a reader. ©1947 by Betty Smith","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Betty Smith’s 1943 novel A Tree Grows in Brooklyn. Francie, a young girl, visits the library often.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Francie thought that all the books in the world were in that library and she had a plan about reading all the books in the world. She","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"was reading a book a day in alphabetical order and not skipping the dry ones. She remembered that the first author had been","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Abbott. She had been reading a book a day for a long time now and she was still in the B’s. Already she had read about bees and","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"buffaloes, Bermuda vacations and Byzantine architecture. For all her enthusiasm, she had to admit that some of the B’s had been","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"hard going. But Francie was a reader.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©1947 by Betty Smith","indent":4}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To illustrate Francie’s enjoyment of an unusual topic","To explain why Francie prefers reading over other activities","To portray Francie’s determination to meet a goal","To describe a book that Francie greatly admires"]},{"id":"e13171c4","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Historians Tiya Miles and Roy E. Finkenbine have both documented the assistance Indigenous peoples gave to Black freedom seekers leaving the South before the US Civil War. Much of the historical evidence of this help comes from Indigenous oral traditions and from autobiographies written by the freedom seekers. One such narrative is Jermain Loguen’s autobiography, which tells about how Neshnabé (Potawatomi) villagers offered him food, lodging, and directions during his 1835 journey from Tennessee to Canada.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Historians Tiya Miles and Roy E. Finkenbine have both documented the assistance Indigenous peoples gave to Black freedom seekers leaving","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the South before the US Civil War. Much of the historical evidence of this help comes from Indigenous oral traditions and from autobiographies","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"written by the freedom seekers. One such narrative is Jermain Loguen’s autobiography, which tells about how Neshnabé (Potawatomi) villagers","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"offered him food, lodging, and directions during his 1835 journey from Tennessee to Canada.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence?","choices":["It provides an example of an autobiography that describes help given by an Indigenous people to a Black freedom seeker.","It shows why Loguen decided to write in great detail about his experiences traveling from Tennessee to Canada in his autobiography.","It argues that autobiographies are particularly important sources of information about geography in the United States before the Civil War.","It suggests that most historians believe that Neshnabé villagers were more successful in assisting freedom seekers than other people were."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["One such narrative is Jermain Loguen’s autobiography, which tells about how Neshnabé (Potawatomi) villagers","offered him food, lodging, and directions during his 1835 journey from Tennessee to Canada."]},{"id":"b2e54b50","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Correlations Between Congestion Ratings and Features of the Crowd in Raters’ Immediate Vicinity Crowd feature Before obstacle After obstacle Overall Density 0.8592 0.7308 0.7447 Velocity −0.9357 −0.9518 −0.8587 Researcher Xiaolu Jia and colleagues monitored individuals’ velocity and the surrounding crowd density as a group of study participants walked through a space and navigated around an obstacle. Participants rated how congested it seemed before the obstacle, after the obstacle, and overall, and the researchers correlated those ratings with velocity and density. (Correlations range from −1 to 1, with greater distance from 0 indicating greater strength). The researchers concluded that the correlations with velocity are stronger than those with density.","passage_lines":[{"type":"table","title":"Correlations Between Congestion Ratings and Features of the Crowd in Raters’ Immediate Vicinity","headers":["Crowd feature","Before obstacle","After obstacle","Overall"],"rows":[["Density","0.8592","0.7308","0.7447"],["Velocity","−0.9357","−0.9518","−0.8587"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Researcher Xiaolu Jia and colleagues monitored individuals’ velocity and the surrounding crowd density as a group of study participants walked through a space and navigated around an obstacle. Participants rated how congested it seemed before the obstacle, after the obstacle, and overall, and the researchers correlated those ratings with velocity and density. (Correlations range from −1 to 1, with greater distance from 0 indicating greater strength). The researchers concluded that the correlations with velocity are stronger than those with density."}],"question":"Which choice best describes data from the table that support the researchers’ conclusion?","choices":["The correlation between congestion ratings before the obstacle and density is further from 0 than the correlation between overall congestion rating and velocity is.","The correlation between congestion ratings before the obstacle and velocity is further from 0 than the correlation between congestion overall and velocity is.","For each of the three ratings, the correlation with velocity is negative while the correlation with density is positive.","For each of the three ratings, correlations with velocity are further from 0 than the corresponding correlations with density are."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["the","Crowd in Raters","Immediate Vicinity"]},{"id":"dc47c2ac","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Although most songbirds build open, cupped nests, some species build domed nests with roofs that provide much more protection. Many ecologists have assumed that domed nests would provide protection from weather conditions and thus would allow species that build them to have larger geographic ranges than species that build open nests do. To evaluate this assumption, a research team led by evolutionary biologist Iliana Medina analyzed data for over 3,000 species of songbirds.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Although most songbirds build open, cupped nests, some species build domed nests with roofs that provide much more protection. Many","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ecologists have assumed that domed nests would provide protection from weather conditions and thus would allow species that build them to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"have larger geographic ranges than species that build open nests do. To evaluate this assumption, a research team led by evolutionary biologist","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Iliana Medina analyzed data for over 3,000 species of songbirds.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding from Medina and her colleagues study, if true, would most directly challenge the assumption in the underlined sentence?","choices":["Species that build open nests tend to have higher extinction rates than species that build domed nests.","Species that build open nests tend to be smaller in size than species that build domed nests.","Species that build open nests tend to use fewer materials to build their nests than species that build domed nests do.","Species that build open nests tend to have larger ranges than species that build domed nests."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Many","ecologists have assumed that domed nests would provide protection from weather conditions and thus would allow species that build them to","have larger geographic ranges than species that build open nests do."]},{"id":"4fc9a13a","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"The novelist Toni Morrison was the first Black woman to work as an editor at the publishing company Random House, from 1967 to 1983. A scholar asserts that one of Morrison’s likely aims during her time as an editor was to strengthen the presence of Black writers on the list of Random House’s published authors.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The novelist Toni Morrison was the first Black woman to work as an editor at the publishing company Random House, from 1967 to 1983. A","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"scholar asserts that one of Morrison’s likely aims during her time as an editor was to strengthen the presence of Black writers on the list of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Random House’s published authors.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most strongly support the scholar’s claim?","choices":["The percentage of authors published by Random House who were Black rose in the early 1970s and stabilized throughout the decade.","Black authors who were interviewed in the 1980s and 1990s were highly likely to cite Toni Morrison’s novels as a principal influence on their work.","The novels written by Toni Morrison that were published after 1983 sold significantly more copies and received wider critical acclaim than the novels she wrote that were published before 1983.","Works that were edited by Toni Morrison during her time at Random House displayed stylistic characteristics that distinguished them from works that were not edited by Morrison."]},{"id":"4987f743","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"ALSOL is a microcredit program in Mexico that makes small loans to female entrepreneurs who lack the collateral and credit history to secure financing from conventional banks. Borrowers use their business proceeds to repay loans in equal weekly installments and incur no penalty for missed payments other than lack of access to larger loans. Economists Gustavo Barboza and Sandra Trejos analyzed ALSOL data and found that rural borrowers, who mostly make and sell handicrafts, miss payments more often than urban borrowers do, partly because they sell their goods less frequently than they could. Barboza and Trejos claim that this behavior reflects strategic decisions that enable rural women to increase their profits per unit sold.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"ALSOL is a microcredit program in Mexico that makes small loans to female entrepreneurs who lack the collateral and credit history to secure","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"financing from conventional banks. Borrowers use their business proceeds to repay loans in equal weekly installments and incur no penalty for","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"missed payments other than lack of access to larger loans. Economists Gustavo Barboza and Sandra Trejos analyzed ALSOL data and found","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that rural borrowers, who mostly make and sell handicrafts, miss payments more often than urban borrowers do, partly because they sell their","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"goods less frequently than they could. Barboza and Trejos claim that this behavior reflects strategic decisions that enable rural women to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"increase their profits per unit sold.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Barboza and Trejos’s claim?","choices":["Many marketplaces require entrepreneurs to pay marketplace operators a fixed percentage of each day’s proceeds in exchange for permission to sell goods there.","Rural entrepreneurs can typically sell their goods for higher prices in cities than in their home areas, but the number of people selling competing goods tends to be higher in cities.","Due to the lower costs they incur, rural entrepreneurs tend to require smaller initial loans than urban entrepreneurs do.","The cost to rural entrepreneurs to bring their goods to towns with marketplaces is high but largely independent of the number of goods they bring."]},{"id":"303bcc41","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Top Four Species of Wild Land Mammals by Global Biomass 3.0 Global biomass (millions 2.5 of metric tons) 2.0 1.5 1.0 0.5 0 t o ar er h an aro bo de ep g ld d el kan wi aile sh ay -t bu gr hite n n w rica ter’s Af ea species Global biomass is the total mass of living material, such as animals and plants, on Earth. A team of scientists estimated the global biomass, by species, of various wild land mammals. The team found that the species with the highest global biomass is the ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Top Four Species of Wild Land Mammals by Global Biomass — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"Global biomass is the total mass of living material, such as animals and plants, on Earth. A team of scientists estimated the global biomass, by species, of various wild land mammals. The team found that the species with the highest global biomass is the ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the sentence?","choices":["wild boar.","eastern gray kangaroo.","African bush elephant.","white-tailed deer."],"unusable":"missing graph"},{"id":"c538954d","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Sense and Sensibility is an 1811 novel by Jane Austen. In the novel, Austen describes Marianne Dashwood’s ability to persuade others of the rightness of her artistic judgments, as is evident when Marianne visits with John Willoughby, a potential suitor: ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Sense and Sensibility is an 1811 novel by Jane Austen. In the novel, Austen describes Marianne Dashwood’s ability to persuade others of the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rightness of her artistic judgments, as is evident when Marianne visits with John Willoughby, a potential suitor: ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from Sense and Sensibility most effectively illustrates the claim?","choices":["“Above all, when she heard him declare, that of music and dancing he was passionately fond, she gave him such a look of approbation as secured the largest share of his discourse to herself for the rest of his stay.”","“Their taste was strikingly alike. The same books, the same passages were idolized by each — or if any difference appeared, any objection” arose, it lasted no longer than till the force of her arguments and the brightness of her eyes could be displayed.","“It was only necessary to mention any favourite amusement to engage her to talk. She could not be silent when such points were introduced, and she had neither shyness nor reserve in their discussion.”","“They speedily discovered that their enjoyment of dancing and music was mutual, and that it arose from a general conformity of judgment in all that related to either. Encouraged by this to a further examination of his opinions, she proceeded to question him on the subject of books.”"]},{"id":"1f3be847","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"“Loon Point” is a 1912 poem by Amy Lowell. In the poem, which presents a nighttime scene on a body of water, Lowell describes an element of nature as an active participant in the experience, writing, ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"“Loon Point” is a 1912 poem by Amy Lowell. In the poem, which presents a nighttime scene on a body of water, Lowell describes an element of","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"nature as an active participant in the experience, writing, ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from “Loon Point” most effectively illustrates the claim?","choices":["“Through the water the moon writes her legends / In light, on the smooth, wet sand.”","“Softly the water ripples / Against the canoe’s curving side.”","“Or like the snow-white petals / Which drop from an overblown rose.”","“But the moon in her wayward beauty / Is ever and always the same.”"]},{"id":"83c9c503","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Nigerian American artist Toyin Ojih Odutola uses black-ink pens to create highly detailed drawings of human figures. Her portrait of novelist Zadie ______ is displayed in the National Portrait Gallery in London.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Nigerian American artist Toyin Ojih Odutola uses black-ink pens to create highly detailed drawings of human figures. Her portrait of novelist","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Zadie ______ is displayed in the National Portrait Gallery in London.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Smith:","Smith —","Smith","Smith,"]},{"id":"eb95235b","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"The Lim ón technique, developed by Mexican-born dancer and choreographer Jose Limón, is known for its emphasis on breath control and its interplay of weight and ______ dancers may explore, for example, the moment of mid-air suspension at the top of a jump.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The Limón technique, developed by Mexican-born dancer and choreographer Jose Limón, is known for its emphasis on breath control and its","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"interplay of weight and ______ dancers may explore, for example, the moment of mid-air suspension at the top of a jump.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["weightlessness","weightlessness which","weightlessness,","weightlessness;"]},{"id":"aecdb820","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Featuring works by the photographers Lola Álvarez Bravo and Else “Yva” Neul ä nder-Simon, the 2021 exhibition The New Woman Behind the Camera set out to provide a wide-ranging overview of photography by women in the 1920s through the ______ given the collection’s breadth of more than 120 photos, its efforts were largely successful.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Featuring works by the photographers Lola Álvarez Bravo and Else “Yva” Neuländer-Simon, the 2021 exhibition The New Woman Behind the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Camera set out to provide a wide-ranging overview of photography by women in the 1920s through the ______ given the collection’s breadth of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"more than 120 photos, its efforts were largely successful.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["1950s, and","1950s and","1950s","1950s,"]},{"id":"2c84f96a","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"In 2017, artists Isabel and Ruben Toledo redesigned the costumes and sets for The Miami City Ballet’s production of The ______ to reviewers, the Toledos’ designs helped infuse the production with elements of Miami’s Latin American culture.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2017, artists Isabel and Ruben Toledo redesigned the costumes and sets for The Miami City Ballet’s production of The______ to reviewers, the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Toledos’ designs helped infuse the production with elements of Miami’s Latin American culture.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Nutcracker according,","Nutcracker , according","Nutcracker according","Nutcracker . According"]},{"id":"7e37affc","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"That the geographic center of North America lay in the state of North Dakota was conceded by all ______ establishing its precise coordinates proved more divisive.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"That the geographic center of North America lay in the state of North Dakota was conceded by all ______ establishing its precise coordinates","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"proved more divisive.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["involved:","involved,","involved","involved;"]},{"id":"96953201","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"In her two major series “Memory Test” and Autobiography, painter Howardena Pindell explored themes ______ healing, self-discovery, and memory by cutting and sewing back together pieces of canvas and inserting personal artifacts, such as postcards, into some of the paintings.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In her two major series “Memory Test” and “Autobiography,” painter Howardena Pindell explored themes ______ healing, self-discovery, and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"memory by cutting and sewing back together pieces of canvas and inserting personal artifacts, such as postcards, into some of the paintings.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["of","of,","of—","of:"]},{"id":"97e2e364","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Okot p Bitek’s poem Song of Lawino (1966) explores postcolonial Ugandan life through the eyes of a woman living in a rural village. With its vibrant imagery, bitingly satiric tone, and dexterous use of traditional Acholi song and phraseology, the poem inspired a generation of East African writers. ______ those who adopted its style are often referred to as Okot School poets.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Okot p’Bitek’s poem Song of Lawino (1966) explores postcolonial Ugandan life through the eyes of a woman living in a rural village. With its","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"vibrant imagery, bitingly satiric tone, and dexterous use of traditional Acholi song and phraseology, the poem inspired a generation of East","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"African writers. ______ those who adopted its style are often referred to as Okot School poets.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Nevertheless,","Fittingly,","By comparison,","Instead,"]},{"id":"bc56170b","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Most, but not all, of the Moon’s oxygen comes from the Sun, via solar wind. Cosmochemist Kentaro Terada from Osaka University wondered if some of the unaccounted-for oxygen could be coming from Earth. In 2008, he analyzed data from the Japanese satellite Kaguya. Kaguya gathered data about gases and particles it encountered while orbiting the Moon. Based on the Kaguya data, Terada confirmed his suspicion that Earth is sending oxygen to the Moon. The student wants to emphasize the aim of the research study.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Most, but not all, of the Moon’s oxygen comes from the Sun, via solar wind.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Cosmochemist Kentaro Terada from Osaka University wondered if some of the unaccounted-for oxygen could be coming from Earth.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"In 2008, he analyzed data from the Japanese satellite Kaguya.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Kaguya gathered data about gases and particles it encountered while orbiting the Moon.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Based on the Kaguya data, Terada confirmed his suspicion that Earth is sending oxygen to the Moon.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["As it orbited the Moon, the Kaguya satellite collected data that was later analyzed by cosmochemist Kentaro Terada.","Before 2008, Kentaro Terada wondered if the Moon was receiving some of its oxygen from Earth.","Cosmochemist Kentaro Terada set out to determine whether some of the Moon’s oxygen was coming from Earth.","Kentaro Terada’s study determined that Earth is sending a small amount of oxygen to the Moon."]},{"id":"6de02dfa","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Thailand’s annual Songkran Water Festival is held each April. It marks Songkran, the traditional Thai New Year. People splash and spray each other for fun at the festival’s community-wide water fights. In Bangkok, thousands gather along Silom Road for the city’s largest water fight. In Chiang Mai, thousands gather at a historical monument called the Tha Phae Gate for the city’s largest water fight. The student wants to emphasize a similarity in how people in Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Thailand’s annual Songkran Water Festival is held each April.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"It marks Songkran, the traditional Thai New Year.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"People splash and spray each other for fun at the festival’s community-wide water fights.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"In Bangkok, thousands gather along Silom Road for the city’s largest water fight.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"In Chiang Mai, thousands gather at a historical monument called the Tha Phae Gate for the city’s largest water fight.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The largest water fight in Bangkok takes place along a city street, whereas the largest water fight in Chiang Mai takes place at a historical monument.","In both Bangkok and Chiang Mai, thousands gather to celebrate Songkran with water fights.","People in both Bangkok and Chiang Mai celebrate Songkran, but they don’t do so in exactly the same way.","Each April, people in Thailand celebrate Songkran, the traditional Thai New Year."]},{"id":"5fa51c86","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Ulaanbaatar is the capital of Mongolia. The city’s population is 907,802. Ulaanbaatar contains 31.98 percent of Mongolia’s population. Hanoi is the capital of Vietnam. The city’s population is 7,781,631. Hanoi contains 8.14 percent of Vietnam’s population. The student wants to emphasize the relative sizes of the two capitals’ populations.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Ulaanbaatar is the capital of Mongolia.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The city’s population is 907,802.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Ulaanbaatar contains 31.98 percent of Mongolia’s population.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Hanoi is the capital of Vietnam.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The city’s population is 7,781,631.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Hanoi contains 8.14 percent of Vietnam’s population.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses information from the given sentences to emphasize the relative sizes of the two capitals’ populations?","choices":["Mongolia’s capital is Ulaanbaatar, which has 907,802 people, and Vietnam’s capital is Hanoi, which has 7,781,631 people.","Comparing Vietnam and Mongolia, 7,781,631 is 8.14 percent of Vietnam’s population, and 907,802 is 31.98 percent of Mongolia’s.","Even though Hanoi (population 7,781,631) is larger than Ulaanbaatar (population 907,802), Ulaanbaatar accounts for more of its country’s population.","The populations of the capitals of Mongolia and Vietnam are 907,802 (Ulaanbaatar) and 7,781,631 (Hanoi), respectively."]},{"id":"290a5d77","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Guard cells are specialized cells that are part of a plant’s pores. These cells help regulate the amount of carbon dioxide a plant takes in. ______ they help regulate a plant’s water loss.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Guard cells are specialized cells that are part of a plant’s pores. These cells help regulate the amount of carbon dioxide a plant takes in. ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"they help regulate a plant’s water loss.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Additionally,","Previously,","In conclusion,","Instead,"]},{"id":"3150021d","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: The Royal Alc ázar of Seville is a historic royal palace in Andalucía, Spain. The palace is famous for its intricate tilework. The palace features majolica and arista tiles. In the majolica style, designs are painted directly on the ceramic tiles. In the arista style, designs are stamped into the ceramic tiles. The student wants to contrast the two styles of tiles.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The Royal Alcázar of Seville is a historic royal palace in Andalucía, Spain.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The palace is famous for its intricate tilework.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"The palace features majolica and arista tiles.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"In the majolica style, designs are painted directly on the ceramic tiles.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"In the arista style, designs are stamped into the ceramic tiles.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Tiles in the majolica and arista styles can be found in the Royal Alc ázar of Seville in Andalucía, Spain.","Featuring tiles in the majolica and arista styles, the Royal Alc ázar of Seville in Spain is famous for its intricate tilework.","In the arista style, designs are stamped into the ceramic tiles, whereas in the majolica style, the designs are painted directly on them.","Among the famous tilework of the Royal Alc ázar of Seville are majolica style tiles, made by painting designs directly on the ceramic tiles."]}];
